Post Date: 2023-01-11T22:54:01Z
Current Date: April 4 2025
Title: Unexpected parent component rerendering
Description: ### Is there an existing issue for this?

- [X] I have searched the existing issues

### Describe the bug

While playing around with some code I noticed a behaviour I wasn't expecting. Here is the code in question:

### Parent Component

```razor
@page "/"

<button @onclick="ShowPrompt">Click me</button>

@if (_showPrompt)
{
    <SurveyPrompt Title="Testing" OnClose="Close" />
}

@code {
    private bool _showPrompt;

    private void ShowPrompt() => _showPrompt = true;
    private void Close() => _showPrompt = false;
}
```

### Child Component

```razor
<div class="alert alert-secondary mt-4">
    <strong>@Title</strong>
    <button @onclick="OnClose">Close</button>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Title { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public Action OnClose { get; set; }
}
```

When clicking the Close button in the child component, the child component causes a re-render in the parent component and is hidden. This is unexpected as that should only occur when either the child components parameter type is `EventCallback` or the handler in the parent calls `StateHasChanged`. 

Changing the child components code to this results in the expected behaviour and the child component isn't hidden.

```razor
<div class="alert alert-secondary mt-4">
    <strong>@Title</strong>
    <button @onclick="() => OnClose()">Close</button>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Title { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public Action OnClose { get; set; }
}
```

I don't know if this is a bug or not but it's not what I was expecting and I can't work it out. 

### Expected Behavior

Child components shouldn't cause re-renders of parents without defining parameters of type `EventCallback` or parent handlers calling `StateHasChanged`

### Steps To Reproduce

Update the `Index` component in a new Blazor project to the following code:

```razor
@page "/"

<button @onclick="ShowPrompt">Click me</button>

@if (_showPrompt)
{
    <SurveyPrompt Title="Testing" OnClose="Close" />
}

@code {
    private bool _showPrompt;

    private void ShowPrompt() => _showPrompt = true;
    private void Close() => _showPrompt = false;
}
```

Update the code for the `SurveyPrompt` component to the following:

```razor
<div class="alert alert-secondary mt-4">
    <strong>@Title</strong>
    <button @onclick="OnClose">Close</button>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Title { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public Action OnClose { get; set; }
}
```

Clicking the button in the index component shows the survey prompt. Clicking the Close button in the SurveyPrompt hides the Survey prompt. However, no StateHasChanged call has been issues.

### Exceptions (if any)

_No response_

### .NET Version

7.0.101

